            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0206" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg124"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890d.00/267: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Beirut</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Knabenshue</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-11-24T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 24,
                                1925—8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your telegram November 23, 6 p.m. The Department realizes that it may be
                    desirable to arrange to have destroyers withdrawn before the new French High
                    Commissioner arrives or at the time of his arrival. The Department, however,
                    before authorizing such action desires to have you give a more detailed report
                    indicating that you believe present conditions are such as fully to justify the
                    departure of the destroyers.</p>
                <p>Alarmist reports still appear in the newspapers regarding the military situation
                    in Syria. It might, therefore, result in misunderstanding in this country should
                    the destroyers be withdrawn. The Department <pb facs="0207" n="125"
                        xml:id="pg125"/> does not desire to give discretionary authority until the
                    reports from you as to the adequacy of measures taken by the French to protect
                    American lives and property are more reassuring.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
